        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 8,
        "titulo": "A profession without «is»",
        "explicacao": "Russian has no «am / is / are» in the present tense, so you simply say «Я врач» (literally «I doctor»). Many profession names have no feminine form and are used for both men and women: «Она врач», «Она инженер». Some do have one: студент → студентка, учитель → учительница.",
